WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Horatio posted
this online recently.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:04.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was a -- This is a famous
"SNL" party, to this day.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Tablegate.
-This is Tablegate.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is me, you...
-Yeah, I look sober there.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...Horatio.
This is Mike Shoemaker.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is --
This was a party that was

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.083
the last Thursday of
the last episode of the season.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we went up into our --
And this is the writer's room.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the 17th floor.
-17th floor at "SNL."

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of the building.
-And this is, like,

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it's normal,
'cause the table's fine.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's called Tablegate --
-For a reason.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.363
-We drank -- We started just
throwing alcohol on the table.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.632
-Yeah. Well, what happened was,
it was a punch bowl.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was very...civil.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:39.339
Very civil.
-And just had punch bowl drinks.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
But now and then, people
spilled a little on the table.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then -- just,
by the end of the night,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
people were just --
it got very --

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.679 size:78% position:39%
there was just drinks
all over the table.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.983
And I thought it'd be funny
if I ran from the hallway

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:53.586 size:84% position:42%
and dove on the table
like a Slip 'N Slide...

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.556
-Yeah.
-...and slide across the table.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did it.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:01.261
On all this alcohol,
I just dove through it and slid.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
it became funny and fun.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
everyone wanted to do it.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then we all did it.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.534
[ Laughter ]
And I remember a friend of ours

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
Andrew Steele
had to stand at this window.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.739
'Cause people would come,
like, sliding this way.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-And catch -- catch --

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.575
-Yeah.
He would literally catch people.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.877 size:81% position:41%
-Or else you'd fly out
a 17th-floor window.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.411 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.381
Somebody's working at their
desk, like, "Jimmy Fallon?"

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Hey, what's up, man?"
I mean, what were we thinking?

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was crazy.
We actually got in

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of trouble
because we broke the table.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was -- It was
my first year on the show,

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:30.557 line:92%
and I had really thought,

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:33.026
"I think you can get fired
for breaking furniture."

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:33.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember that we were
so embarrassed the next day.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were like --
because it was really insane.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.399 line:92%
There were just cups everywhere.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember there was a --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somebody got mad at us
and yelled at us,

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they said,
"Really classy, guys."

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"Really classy move."

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know
what was the extra touch?

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.276 line:92%
It was the towel full of vomit

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of
Carson Daly's office.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"That wasn't me, man."

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"I don't know who did that."

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.450 line:92%
-I do think that's classy.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other thing that's
embarrassing is when you're --

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was literally
my first year on the show,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we used to get free stuff,
and I want to point out --

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:07.861
I don't know if you remember
the 2002 Winter Olympic berets

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
from Salt Lake City.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.599
Literally wearing a free --
-That's some good style.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a good, good style.
-Oh, gosh.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.437 size:75% position:38%
-Like you mentioned,
both have two kids.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You got two girls.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I got two boys.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:24.144
What made you write a book
about making a first child --

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:24.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a first word dada.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was your baby's
first words?

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember?
-I think it was "mama."

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course it was.
Yeah, it is.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just is.
And I know it's an unwritten

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of contest
that husbands have with wives.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you go, "No, that's great.
It could be any word."

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.556 size:84% position:42%
But I really wanted her
to say "dada" first.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I was just
trying to trick her.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anything I would give her --
I mean, I was --

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.762
I would give her a bottle
and go, "Do you want dada?

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want a dada?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't care
if the baby is stupid,

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want,
for the history books --

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's up to someone else
to fix my baby.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just wanted,
for the history books,

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.239 line:92%
that first word was "dada."

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I put the book out,
and it was funny, as a joke.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
people started actually

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.545 line:92%
really reading it with the kids.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, kids started reading
it back to their parents,

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.283 line:92%
and it became a cool thing.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so they said,
"You should make mama."

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like -- And
it's clearly written by me

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause there's only like
10 words in the book.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"Mama, quack, mama, moo."

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It's not ghost written.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where do you get your ideas?!
-Oh, just over a text!

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I put out "Mama,"
and I figured,

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
since women
are smarter than men,

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.469 size:84% position:42%
mamas, they don't care.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-'Cause they are.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is correct.
-They don't care about

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.041
if the baby says "mama or dada"
in the sequel.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's called
"Everything is Mama."

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.277
In that one,
the mama's trying to teach kids

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there are other words.
-Oh, I see.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:36.916
-So it's like "Balloon," things
like noodles, stuff like that.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.319
And then the baby just keeps
saying, "Mama, Mama, Mama."

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, anyways, yeah.
I'm writing a lot of books.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-I'm an author now.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, that's great.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we love
having authors on the show.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:51.331
-Hey, I just want to say, dude,
I watch you every night,

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I watched you
since you began.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're doing such a great job
on the show.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everyone here really --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
Job well done, dude.
-I really appreciate it.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you for handing it over.
It's an honor to do it.

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for Jimmy Fallon,
everybody!

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"The Tonight Show"!

